# electron-updater + electron-builder Research for LexPro

## Project context confirmed
- **electron-updater latest version: 6.8.9** (verified via `npm view electron-updater version`). It has **no peer dependencies** — it bundles everything (`builder-util-runtime`, `js-yaml`, `semver`, etc.), so installation is standalone.
- Main process: `C:\Users\Mahmoud\Desktop\LexPro\packages\main\src\index.ts` — already uses `const isDev = !app.isPackaged;` (line 26) and IPC handlers via `ipcMain.handle(...)`.
- Preload: `C:\Users\Mahmoud\Desktop\LexPro\packages\main\src\preload.ts` — exposes `window.electronAPI` via `contextBridge.exposeInMainWorld`.
- Renderer types: `C:\Users\Mahmoud\Desktop\LexPro\packages\renderer\src\electron.d.ts` — declares the `Window.electronAPI` interface.
- electron-builder.json at root uses `appId: "com.lexpro.app"`, NSIS Windows target, output `dist-electtron`.
- Renderer consumes via optional chaining `window.electronAPI?.method()` (seen in `CustomerDossier.tsx`, `Templates.tsx`).

---

## 1. Install electron-updater

It is a **runtime dependency** (runs in the packaged main process), so install it in the main workspace:

```bash
npm install electron-updater -w @lexpro/main
```

This adds it to `packages/main/package.json` `dependencies`. Because the root `electron-builder.json` `files` array includes `node_modules/**/*`, it will be packaged into the build automatically. (Version resolves to `^6.8.9`.)

---

## 2. electron-builder.json — GitHub Releases publish config

Add a top-level `publish` array. The current file needs this block added (appId, productName, win, nsis blocks stay as-is):

```json
{
  "appId": "com.lexpro.app",
  "productName": "LEX PRO",
  "directories": {
    "output": "dist-electron"
  },
  "publish": [
    {
      "provider": "github",
      "owner": "<your-github-username-or-org>",
      "repo": "lexpro",
      "releaseType": "release",
      "vPrefixedTagName": true
    }
  ],
  "files": [
    "packages/main/dist/**/*",
    "packages/renderer/dist/**/*",
    "packages/server/dist/**/*",
    "node_modules/**/*"
  ],
  "win": {
    "target": "nsis",
    "icon": "build/icon.ico"
  },
  "nsis": {
    "oneClick": false,
    "allowToChangeInstallationDirectory": true,
    "createDesktopShortcut": true,
    "shortcutName": "LEX PRO"
  }
}
```

Notes:
- `owner`/`repo` must match your GitHub repo. electron-builder auto-generates `latest.yml` in `dist-electron/` which electron-updater fetches at runtime.
- To publish, run with the `GH_TOKEN` env var set: `$env:GH_TOKEN="ghp_xxx"; npm run package -- --publish always` (PowerShell). Without `--publish`, it just builds locally.
- electron-updater reads `latest.yml` (Windows) — this is produced automatically by electron-builder when the `publish` provider is `github`.

---

## 3. Main process auto-update code (`packages/main/src/index.ts`)

Add the import and an `initAutoUpdater()` function. Wire it into the existing `app.whenReady().then(...)`. Key points: only run when `app.isPackaged` (production); emit events to renderer via `mainWindow.webContents.send(...)`.

```ts
import { app, BrowserWindow, shell, ipcMain, dialog } from 'electron';
import { autoUpdater, UpdateCheckResult, UpdateInfo } from 'electron-updater';
import * as path from 'path';
import * as fs from 'fs';

let mainWindow: BrowserWindow | null = null;

// ... existing createWindow() stays the same ...

function initAutoUpdater(): void {
  // Only packaged apps support auto-update; skip in dev
  if (!app.isPackaged) {
    console.log('[autoUpdater] Skipping in development mode');
    return;
  }

  // (Optional) disable auto-download if you want explicit user consent first:
  // autoUpdater.autoDownload = false;

  // Auto-install on quit once downloaded (default is true)
  autoUpdater.autoInstallOnAppQuit = true;

  // ---- Forward every event to the renderer for UI notifications ----
  autoUpdater.on('checking-for-update', () => {
    mainWindow?.webContents.send('update-status', { event: 'checking-for-update' });
  });

  autoUpdater.on('update-available', (info: UpdateInfo) => {
    mainWindow?.webContents.send('update-status', {
      event: 'update-available',
      version: info.version,
      releaseNotes: info.releaseNotes,
    });
  });

  autoUpdater.on('update-not-available', (info: UpdateInfo) => {
    mainWindow?.webContents.send('update-status', { event: 'update-not-available' });
  });

  autoUpdater.on('download-progress', (progress) => {
    mainWindow?.webContents.send('update-status', {
      event: 'download-progress',
      percent: progress.percent,
      transferred: progress.transferred,
      total: progress.total,
    });
  });

  autoUpdater.on('update-downloaded', (info: UpdateInfo) => {
    mainWindow?.webContents.send('update-status', {
      event: 'update-downloaded',
      version: info.version,
      releaseNotes: info.releaseNotes,
    });
  });

  autoUpdater.on('error', (err: Error) => {
    mainWindow?.webContents.send('update-status', {
      event: 'error',
      message: err?.message ?? String(err),
    });
  });

  // IPC: renderer can request install-and-restart now
  ipcMain.handle('install-update', () => {
    // quitAndInstall() restarts the app after installing
    autoUpdater.quitAndInstall(false, true);
  });

  // IPC: renderer can trigger a manual check
  ipcMain.handle('check-for-updates', async () => {
    try {
      const result: UpdateCheckResult | null = await autoUpdater.checkForUpdates();
      return { success: true, updateAvailable: !!result?.updateInfo };
    } catch (err) {
      return { success: false, message: (err as Error).message };
    }
  });

  // Check for updates on app start (after a short delay to let window load)
  // autoDownload defaults to true, so it downloads automatically when available.
  setTimeout(() => {
    autoUpdater.checkForUpdates().catch((err) => {
      console.error('[autoUpdater] checkForUpdates failed:', err);
    });
  }, 3000);
}

app.whenReady().then(() => {
  createWindow();
  initAutoUpdater(); // <-- add this

  app.on('activate', () => {
    if (BrowserWindow.getAllWindows().length === 0) {
      createWindow();
    }
  });
});
```

**Behavior summary:**
- Checks ~3s after startup → if newer version on GitHub Releases, downloads automatically (`autoDownload` default true).
- Emits `update-downloaded` → renderer shows a notification.
- User clicks "Install & restart" → calls `install-update` IPC → `autoUpdater.quitAndInstall(false, true)`.
- If user ignores it, `autoInstallOnAppQuit = true` installs silently when they quit normally.

---

## 4. Preload (`packages/main/src/preload.ts`) — expose events to renderer

Add a one-way listener channel and two invoke handlers. Add to the existing `contextBridge.exposeInMainWorld('electronAPI', {...})`:

```ts
import { contextBridge, ipcRenderer } from 'electron';

contextBridge.exposeInMainWorld('electronAPI', {
  savePDF: (html: string, fileName: string) =>
    ipcRenderer.invoke('save-pdf', html, fileName),
  printDocument: (html: string) =>
    ipcRenderer.invoke('print-document', html),
  printFile: (url: string) =>
    ipcRenderer.invoke('print-file', url),
  openFile: (url: string, title: string) =>
    ipcRenderer.invoke('open-file', url, title),

  // ---- Auto-update bridge ----
  checkForUpdates: () => ipcRenderer.invoke('check-for-updates'),
  installUpdate: () => ipcRenderer.invoke('install-update'),
  // Subscribe to update-status events from main; returns an unsubscribe fn
  onUpdateStatus: (callback: (status: UpdateStatus) => void) => {
    const handler = (_event: unknown, status: UpdateStatus) => callback(status);
    ipcRenderer.on('update-status', handler);
    return () => ipcRenderer.removeListener('update-status', handler);
  },
});
```

The `UpdateStatus` type (add to `electron.d.ts`, next section) represents the payloads sent from main.

---

## 5. Renderer types (`packages/renderer/src/electron.d.ts`) — extend the interface

Add the update API to the existing `Window.electronAPI` declaration:

```ts
export {};

export type UpdateEvent =
  | 'checking-for-update'
  | 'update-available'
  | 'update-not-available'
  | 'download-progress'
  | 'update-downloaded'
  | 'error';

export interface UpdateStatus {
  event: UpdateEvent;
  version?: string;
  releaseNotes?: string | unknown;
  percent?: number;
  transferred?: number;
  total?: number;
  message?: string;
}

declare global {
  interface Window {
    electronAPI?: {
      savePDF: (html: string, fileName: string) => Promise<{ success: boolean; message: string }>;
      printDocument: (html: string) => Promise<{ success: boolean; message: string }>;
      printFile: (url: string) => Promise<{ success: boolean; message: string }>;
      openFile: (url: string, title: string) => Promise<{ success: boolean; message: string }>;

      // Auto-update
      checkForUpdates: () => Promise<{ success: boolean; updateAvailable?: boolean; message?: string }>;
      installUpdate: () => Promise<void>;
      onUpdateStatus: (callback: (status: UpdateStatus) => void) => () => void;
    };
  }
}
```

---

## Renderer UI pattern (React component example)

A minimal notification component using the bridge. Place anywhere in `packages/renderer/src`:

```tsx
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
import type { UpdateStatus } from '../electron'; // adjust path if re-exported

export function UpdateNotification() {
  const [status, setStatus] = useState<UpdateStatus | null>(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!window.electronAPI?.onUpdateStatus) return;
    const unsubscribe = window.electronAPI.onUpdateStatus((s) => setStatus(s));
    return unsubscribe; // cleanup on unmount
  }, []);

  if (!status || !window.electronAPI) return null;

  if (status.event === 'update-downloaded') {
    return (
      <div className="update-toast">
        <p>الإصدار {status.version} جاهز للتثبيت</p>
        <button onClick={() => window.electronAPI!.installUpdate()}>
          تثبيت وإعادة التشغيل
        </button>
      </div>
    );
  }

  if (status.event === 'download-progress' && typeof status.percent === 'number') {
    return <div className="update-toast">جاري تنزيل التحديث: {Math.round(status.percent)}%</div>;
  }

  return null;
}
```

---

## 6. Development vs Production considerations

- **`autoUpdater` ONLY works in a packaged (built) app.** It relies on `app-update.yml` embedded by electron-builder in `resources/app-update.yml` (Windows) and on code-signing metadata. Calling it in dev throws `Error: Update is not available...` / cannot read `app-update.yml`.
- The code guards this with `if (!app.isPackaged) return;` at the top of `initAutoUpdater()`. The project already uses this same `!app.isPackaged` check (index.ts line 26).
